@startuml campusclaw_tdd_agent_architecture
title CampusClaw TDD Agent Architecture

' Design baseline: pi-mono-java-design commit d2b9b4b6f4762e0e9734c144e3eb3273959e7e26.
' Code baseline: pi-mono-java commit ae0ae7c164b031afacd862794e8914243913f113.
' Source paths: modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/CampusClawAiService.java.
' Source paths: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java.
' Source paths: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java.
' Source paths: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts.
' Observed behavior: current tests cover many modules, while CI runs only Maven verify and the legacy agent covers Runtime HTTP.
' Design reason: an independent Codex quality engineer must maintain product knowledge and tests while deterministic executors decide pass or fail.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #35516F
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial

actor "Product Designer" as designer
actor "Product Developer" as developer
cloud "Pull Request, Push, and Schedule Events" as events

package "Independent Codex Quality Engineer" {
  component "CampusClaw TDD Skill" as skill
  component "Capability Inventory Sync" as inventory
  component "Requirement and Risk Analyst" as analyst
  component "Test Maintenance Planner" as maintainer
  component "Failure Triage and Report" as triage
}

database "Capability Registry and Traceability Graph" as registry
artifact "Accepted Design Contracts" as designs
artifact "Implementation Source and Change Diff" as source

package "Deterministic Automation Platform" {
  component "Impact Selector" as selector
  component "Java and Contract Adapter" as java
  component "OpenGauss and Process Adapter" as process
  component "Frontend and Browser Adapter" as frontend
  component "Fault and Mutation Adapter" as fault
  component "Evidence and Verdict Engine" as verdict
}

node "Isolated Git Worktree" as worktree
artifact "Test-only Draft Pull Request" as testpr
artifact "Capability Health Report" as report

designer --> designs : reviewed behavior
developer --> source : candidate change
events --> skill : trigger mode
designs --> inventory
source --> inventory
skill --> inventory
inventory --> registry : versioned knowledge
registry --> analyst
designs --> analyst
source --> analyst
analyst --> selector : impact and required suites
analyst --> maintainer : missing or stale coverage
maintainer --> worktree : tests, fixtures, registry only
worktree --> testpr
selector --> java
selector --> process
selector --> frontend
selector --> fault
java --> verdict
process --> verdict
frontend --> verdict
fault --> verdict
verdict --> triage
registry --> triage
triage --> report
triage --> maintainer : reproducible test gap

note right of registry
  Product knowledge is persistent and reviewable.
  Chat memory is never the source of truth.
end note

note right of verdict
  Checked-in assertions and contracts decide results.
  The model explains evidence but cannot waive failures.
end note

note bottom of maintainer
  The agent may change test assets and propose a draft PR.
  It may not change product code, weaken assertions, or merge.
end note
@enduml

@startuml design_to_test_maintenance
title Design-to-Test Maintenance Loop

' Design baseline: pi-mono-java-design commit d2b9b4b6f4762e0e9734c144e3eb3273959e7e26.
' Code baseline: pi-mono-java commit ae0ae7c164b031afacd862794e8914243913f113.
' Design paths: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-http-v1-design.md and pi-mono-java-tool-system/README.md.
' Test paths: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/test/java and modules/agent-core/src/test/java.
' Observed behavior: design versions and implementation tests evolve independently and exact requirement-to-test binding is incomplete.
' Design reason: mature requirements must create executable red tests before product implementation, while proposals must not block delivery.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial

actor "Designer or Developer" as author
participant "TDD Agent" as agent
database "Capability Registry" as registry
participant "Design Maturity Gate" as maturity
participant "Coverage Analyzer" as coverage
participant "Test Worktree" as worktree
participant "Deterministic Runner" as runner
participant "Human Reviewer" as reviewer

author -> agent : design or code change
agent -> registry : refresh source evidence and hashes
agent -> maturity : classify each changed requirement

alt proposed or research-only requirement
  maturity --> agent : advisory only
  agent -> registry : record target and open question
else accepted, frozen, or implemented requirement
  maturity --> agent : enforceable requirement
  agent -> coverage : resolve requirement to cases and selectors
  alt exact executable coverage exists
    coverage --> agent : reuse or update impacted tests
  else coverage missing or stale
    coverage --> agent : coverage gap
    agent -> worktree : add failing tests and fixtures
    worktree -> reviewer : test-only draft pull request
  end
  agent -> runner : execute selected mandatory suites
  runner --> agent : evidence, seed, logs, and verdict
  agent -> registry : bind requirement, case, selector, and run
  agent -> reviewer : analysis report and recommended action
end

note over agent,runner
  Unmapped accepted P0 behavior is a failed coverage gate.
  Environment failure is blocked, never passed or skipped.
end note
@enduml

@startuml realtime_and_scheduled_detection
title Real-time and Scheduled Detection

' Code baseline: pi-mono-java commit ae0ae7c164b031afacd862794e8914243913f113.
' CI path: .github/workflows/ci.yml lines 4-26.
' Frontend paths: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts and frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts.
' Observed behavior: pull requests and pushes run Maven verification, but frontend and deep environment suites are not required.
' Design reason: event-driven deterministic gates provide near-real-time detection, while Codex scheduled tasks perform deeper maintenance and triage.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #35516F
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial

cloud "Pull Request or Push" as change
cloud "Nightly Schedule" as nightly
cloud "Release Candidate" as release

component "Change Gate: seconds to minutes" as fast
component "Independent Codex TDD Task: inventory and maintenance" as agent
component "Nightly Deep Regression: full, fault, concurrency" as deep
component "Release Qualification: packaged and mirror checks" as qualification

database "Capability Registry" as registry
artifact "Required Check" as check
artifact "Test Maintenance Draft PR" as pr
artifact "Evidence Bundle and Health Report" as evidence

change --> fast
registry --> fast : impact map and mandatory suites
fast --> check
fast --> evidence

nightly --> agent
registry --> agent
agent --> deep
deep --> evidence
agent --> pr : only when coverage changes

release --> qualification
registry --> qualification
qualification --> evidence
qualification --> check

note right of fast
  This is code-change near-real-time detection.
  It does not claim production health monitoring.
end note

note right of agent
  A standalone task gets a fresh isolated worktree.
  The repository skill restores the same engineering workflow.
end note
@enduml
